        "question": {
          ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(1,1,1)$ to $(4,3,3).$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "For scalar arc length, use\n\n$$\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nParametrize the segment and check its endpoints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r(t)&=A+t(B-A) \\\\  &=\\left(3 t + 1,2 t + 1,2 t + 1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(0)&=\\left(1,1,1\\right) \\\\  \\mathbf r(1)&=\\left(4,3,3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le t\\le1$, the velocity and speed are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\left(3,2,2\\right) \\\\  \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(3)^2+(2)^2+(2)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute all three coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=(3 t + 1)(2 t + 1)^2 \\\\  &=12 t^{3} + 16 t^{2} + 7 t + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate the expanded polynomial and subtract the endpoint values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\sqrt{17}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12 t^{3} + 16 t^{2} + 7 t + 1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  &=\\sqrt{17}\\left[3 t^{4} + \\frac{16 t^{3}}{3} + \\frac{7 t^{2}}{2} + t\\right]_0^1 \\\\  &=\\sqrt{17}\\left(\\left(\\frac{77}{6}\\right)-(0)\\right) \\\\  &=\\frac{77 \\sqrt{17}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
